      "description": "The only specification naming skill 'dev' is docs/specs/dev-skill-spec.md. It specifies a Codex skill and its authoring-metadata table names C:\\Projects\\DevForgeAI\\src\\agents\\skills\\dev as the final development package. The assessed Claude Code package at .claude/skills/dev is a derived port of that package, and no specification in the repository governs it. Eight of its eleven files are byte-identical to the Codex parent; the three that differ carry every host-specific decision, including the defective passage in the companion finding. No builder authoring record accompanied the port, so its history is inferred from the byte delta rather than verified (ORG-U4).\n\nTwo adjacent observations are recorded but are not package defects. The specification's frontmatter reads status: proposed and package_status: not_authored while three copies of the package exist on disk; repository instructions already record that frontmatter as stale. And the validator's bounded lookup roots, docs/plan and docs/design/specs, do not contain this specification - docs/design/specs does not exist - which the specification itself anticipates by naming its own absolute path and noting that builder lookup searches elsewhere. Absence from the lookup roots was therefore not treated as absence, and no origin specification was reconstructed.",
      "user_impact": "Host-specific port decisions have no contract to be assessed against, so conformance for those three files can only be judged against general Claude Code guidance. That is precisely where the one real defect in this package was introduced and would not have been caught by specification conformance.",
